Subject: [PATCH 45/53] drama: voices say whose they are, takes are prepared
 and gated, GET /v1/voices lists them

A voice file carries source {kind: model-invented | owner | consented, note}, and --voices refuses a file without one. drama_voice_clip.py turns a take into a mono 44.1 kHz clip at one speech level, cut at a pause to 10-30 s, refusing clipping, noise, music or hum and a second speaker; its transcript is the take's only when the cut keeps all the speech, else a local Whisper draft to correct. drama_voice.py encodes with tensorfold-native voice encode when present, else the reference's encoder, and writes the source either way. GET /v1/voices lists the loaded voices; encoding stays offline.
